{
 "annotations": {
  "destructiveHint": false,
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": false,
  "title": "Propose what a workflow's steps take"
 },
 "description": "Propose estimates from what someone said, as ranges \u2014 people know \"20 minutes to an hour\", not \"37 minutes\"; when they give one number, use it for both ends. Each item is either a `measure` or a `gate` on a step (nodeId from compass_workflow_steps):\n- measure.metric `working`: hands-on minutes per run (low/high).\n- measure.metric `waiting`: minutes the work sits idle before or inside the step \u2014 ask about this separately; it's usually most of the waste.\n- measure.metric `hardCost`: money that isn't anyone's time (amount, currency, per run or month).\n- measure.metric `frequency` with nodeId null: how often the workflow runs (low/high per day, week, month, or year); with variantId, how often that variant runs.\n- gate: approval, handoff, rekey (typing the same data into another system), or rework, with returnRate (0\u20131) when they know how often it sends work back.\nPass subjectPageId (a ROLE or PERSON) when the time is one person's or role's \u2014 it prices the time through that role's rate. Always say who said it. Proposals count once someone accepts them in Compass.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "properties": {
   "items": {
    "items": {
     "properties": {
      "gate": {
       "properties": {
        "gate": {
         "enum": [
          "approval",
          "handoff",
          "rekey",
          "rework"
         ],
         "type": "string"
        },
        "returnRate": {
         "maximum": 1,
         "minimum": 0,
         "type": "number"
        }
       },
